{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "AgentBase Runtime API",
    "description": "Managed compute service for running containerized AI agents. It handles deploying, scaling, and routing requests to your agent containers, so you can focus on building the agent logic itself.\n\n## Authentication\nEvery request must carry a VNG Cloud IAM OAuth2 access token in the `Authorization` header as `Bearer <access_token>`. Use the **Authorize** button above to set it for \"Try it out\" calls. The gateway validates the token and enforces fine-grained IAM permissions on the **Agent Runtime** resource.\n\n## Core concepts\n- **Runtime**: a logical AI-agent application you own. Creating one provisions a container registry repository and an IAM Service Account for the agent.\n- **Version**: an immutable snapshot of a runtime's configuration (image, env vars, startup command, flavor, autoscaling). Numbered from 1; updating a runtime always creates a new version.\n- **Endpoint**: a live deployment of a specific version that actually serves traffic and exposes a public URL. The auto-created `DEFAULT` endpoint always tracks the latest version.\n- **Flavor**: a named compute size (CPU/RAM/GPU) an endpoint runs on.\n\nSee the full User Guide for end-to-end examples.",
    "contact": {
      "name": "GreenNode AI Platform",
      "url": "https://aiplatform.console.greennode.ai/agent-runtime"
    },
    "version": "v1"
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "https://agentbase.api.vngcloud.vn/runtime"
    }
  ],
  "security": [
    {
      "bearerAuth": []
    }
  ],
  "tags": [
    {
      "name": "Agent Runtimes",
      "description": "Manage AI-agent runtimes, their immutable versions, and the endpoints that deploy those versions to serve traffic."
    },
    {
      "name": "Flavors",
      "description": "Catalog of available compute sizes (CPU/RAM/GPU) that a runtime endpoint can be deployed on."
    },
    {
      "name": "Runtime Traces",
      "description": "Query distributed traces emitted by agent runtimes (backed by Tempo). Query parameters are forwarded to the tracing backend, so its query syntax applies."
    },
    {
      "name": "OpenClaw Versions",
      "description": "The catalog of published OpenClaw versions that instances can be pinned to."
    },
    {
      "name": "OpenClaw",
      "description": "Manage OpenClaw agent instances: create, run, and pin them to a published OpenClaw version."
    }
  ],
